@meta
id: 07-17
title: Drill — bracket to bracket, semicolon
chapter: 07
type: drill
skills: match-percent
par: 46
minutes: 4
reps: 10
vscode: six scrolls and six clicks on the closing brace
open: registry.ts

@brief
Six container registrations, none of them terminated. Semicolon on the
closing bracket of each.

Nothing to work out. The dojo will hand you the file ten times.

@keys
| `%` | jump to the matching bracket |
| `A` | append at the end of the line |
| `2j` | down two lines |

@hints
The rep is `%` to the closing bracket, `A` `;` `Esc`, then `2j` to the top
of the next registration.
--
Do not look at where `%` put you. That is the habit being drilled: you
trust the match rather than checking it.

@solution
    % A ; <Esc> 2j    six times, then :wq<Enter>

Thirty-eight keystrokes for six terminations.

These blocks are three lines long, so `%` looks like an expensive way to
press `jj`. It is not, and the reason is that `%` does not change when the
block does. Add a second `useClass` line, wrap one registration in a
factory, and `jj` is wrong everywhere while `%` is still right everywhere.

The drill is really about trust. Beginners press `%`, look at where they
landed, and check the indentation — which costs more than the keystroke
saved. Landing correctly a hundred times in a row is what stops you
checking.

@start registry.ts
container.register(OrderRepository, {
  useClass: OrderRepository,
})

container.register(OrderProvider, {
  useClass: OrderProvider,
})

container.register(RefundRepository, {
  useClass: RefundRepository,
})

container.register(RefundProvider, {
  useClass: RefundProvider,
})

container.register(PaymentService, {
  useClass: HttpPaymentService,
})

container.register(EmailService, {
  useClass: SmtpEmailService,
})

@expected registry.ts
container.register(OrderRepository, {
  useClass: OrderRepository,
});

container.register(OrderProvider, {
  useClass: OrderProvider,
});

container.register(RefundRepository, {
  useClass: RefundRepository,
});

container.register(RefundProvider, {
  useClass: RefundProvider,
});

container.register(PaymentService, {
  useClass: HttpPaymentService,
});

container.register(EmailService, {
  useClass: SmtpEmailService,
});
